Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:39:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] ozone: link without X11 when Qt has GLX

The engine fails to link where webengine_ozone_x11 is off and Qt's
xcb_glx_plugin is on, as both of Omaweb's builds are: undefined
GLXHelper::instance(). GbmBufferFactory::instance() asks for the GLX
helper under xcb_glx_plugin alone, while glx_helper.cpp is compiled only
with ozone X11.

This is Qt's own change to the same line, backported unchanged. It is
on dev and picked to 6.12, but not on the 6.140.0 release. It drops when
the series moves to an engine that carries it.

qtwebengine ca137f50ec704caecba07f8c4a30fb046999ce02:
Change-Id: I636220cddca993cf534253d0228852ef7eed4e77

omaweb#484

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/ozone/gbm_buffer_factory.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/ozone/gbm_buffer_factory.cpp b/src/core/ozone/gbm_buffer_factory.cpp
index 4b72b5fe2b..3a315c59cc 100644
--- a/src/core/ozone/gbm_buffer_factory.cpp
+++ b/src/core/ozone/gbm_buffer_factory.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include "ozone/glx_helper.h"
 #include "ozone/ozone_util_qt.h"
 
+#include "ui/base/ozone_buildflags.h"
 #include "ui/gfx/buffer_format_util.h"
 #include "ui/gfx/linux/drm_util_linux.h"
 #include "ui/gfx/linux/gbm_buffer.h"
@@ -70,7 +71,7 @@ static base::ScopedFD openDrmNodePath(const std::string &path)
 
 GbmBufferFactory *GbmBufferFactory::instance()
 {
-#if QT_CONFIG(xcb_glx_plugin)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OZONE_X11) && QT_CONFIG(xcb_glx_plugin)
     if (OzoneUtilQt::usingGLX())
         return GLXHelper::instance()->gbmFactory();
 #endif
